<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malwa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malwa is a region of west-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on a plateau north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narmada-river">Narmada</a> river. It was a fertile and strategically placed territory contested by successive powers. In the eighteenth century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> conquered Malwa from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>, and it became a base for Maratha expansion northwards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malwa.jpg" alt="Malwa" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fielding Lucas, Jr. · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Malwa_India_closeup_1823.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
